cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CP2K-FORGE"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sharma
    given-names: Dhruv
    affiliation: "University of Cambridge"
abstract: >-
  CP2K-FORGE (Foundation-model Optimisation of Reference Generation and
  Evaluation in CP2K) forges compact, system-specific MACE interatomic
  potentials: a MACE foundation model proposes configurations, CP2K labels
  them with DFT single points (semi-local or hybrid revPBE0-D3/ADMM), and a
  small MACE is trained from scratch on those labels, iterating under
  force-accuracy and own-MD stability checks until a stop rule fires.
  Developed for the MPhil thesis "Machine-Learned Interatomic Potentials in
  CP2K" (University of Cambridge, 2026).
keywords:
  - machine-learned interatomic potentials
  - CP2K
  - MACE
  - active learning
  - molecular dynamics
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DhruvSkyy/cp2k-forge"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: 2026-10-10
